{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.229, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 27, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:06.091Z", "t_ms": 5100, "delta": "Self-RAG decides when to retrieve dynamically by predicting a special reflection token called `Retrieve` at"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.312, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 28, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:06.255Z", "t_ms": 5264, "delta": " each segment step [C1, C2, C5]:\n\n* **Token-based Prediction:** Given the input prompt $"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.436, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 29, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:06.378Z", "t_ms": 5387, "delta": "x$ and the preceding generation $y_{<t}$, the generator language model evaluates whether the continuation requires factual grounding and"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.609, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 30, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:06.550Z", "t_ms": 5559, "delta": " decodes a `Retrieve` token from three possible values: `{yes, no, continue}` [C2, C7]. "}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.727, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 31, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:06.665Z", "t_ms": 5674, "delta": "\n  * `yes` indicates that retrieval is required to supply external knowledge [C2, C7].\n  *"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 5.868, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 32, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:06.810Z", "t_ms": 5819, "delta": " `no` indicates retrieval is unnecessary because the continuation does not require factual grounding or would not be improved by external evidence [C7].\n  "}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.15, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 33, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:07.057Z", "t_ms": 6066, "delta": "* `continue` indicates that the model can continue using evidence retrieved in a previous step without fetching new passages [C7"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.502, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 34, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:07.424Z", "t_ms": 6433, "delta": "].\n\n* **Execution Modes at Inference:**\n  * **Hard Decision:** If the model directly outputs `Retrieve == Yes`, the retriever fetches"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.695, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 35, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:07.637Z", "t_ms": 6646, "delta": " relevant passages; if `Retrieve == No`, the model generates the next segment directly without retrieval, operating like a standard language model [C"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 6.891, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 36, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:07.832Z", "t_ms": 6841, "delta": "2, C3].\n  * **Threshold-based (Soft) Retrieval:** Alternatively, a threshold can be specified during inference ["}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.057, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 37, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:07.996Z", "t_ms": 7006, "delta": "C5]. If the probability of generating `Retrieve = Yes` (normalized over all possible `Retrieve` tokens) exceeds"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.229, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 38, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:08.170Z", "t_ms": 7179, "delta": " this designated threshold, retrieval is triggered [C5]. This allows tuning retrieval frequency depending on task demands (e.g., retrieving more often"}}
{"event": "token", "client_s": 7.448, "data": {"request_id": "c2f63e1dcc79", "seq": 39, "ts": "2026-10-28T04:33:08.390Z", "t_ms": 7399, "delta": " for fact-heavy tasks versus less often for creative or open-ended tasks) [C5]."}}
